{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777814-spirit-slayers","id":777814,"title":"Spirit Slayers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T10:20:21-08:00","id":777814,"title":"Spirit Slayers","content":"So, I was reading through Spirit Slayers for the first time, and I came away with a couple of insights. Notably, that the 'Dominions' of werewolves in that book look quite similar to some Facets of Gifts in Forsaken 2E, and that others could be adapted to make some pretty cool Rites.<br /> <br /> Secondly, did anyone else find Spirits as presented in Spirit Slayers to be a heck of a lot more powerful than Spirits in the W:tF corebooks or other source material featuring Spirits? Its chart for statting out Spirits on pg. 181 seems to track with 'baseline' Spirit power levels up until Rank 3, when they start to expand outwards in a big way. Six dots of Influence to divide between up to four Influences. Rank 5 Spirits get 15 dots of Influence to spread across up to 12 Influences. This isn't necessarily a bad thing, personally I think Spirits that hit Rank 3 and start becoming movers and shakers in the local Shadow probably should start to break away from the general populace in terms of power, and seeing Rank 5 Spirits possessed of a range of powers befitting a minor god is really cool, but it just jumped out at me as a little unusual.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever used this chart in-game? How have Spirits using these guidelines played out compared to Spirits as written in other source material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":".  Got the page number wrong, originally wrote it down as 131 12-03-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:26:55-08:00","id":779022,"title":"","content":"I can't find this chart you speak of anywhere in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:21:26-08:00","id":779107,"title":"","content":"It's on page 181.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:18:08-08:00","id":779165,"title":"","content":"Whoops, my bad. Yeah, it's page 181. I wasn't looking terribly closely and with that font the 8 looked like a 3 to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:38:33-08:00","id":779185,"title":"","content":"It's probably important to note that the influences in Spirit slayers don't quite work like influences elsewhere. They pull double duty as skills, and the dice pool to use them in the normal manner is smaller than standard, being one attribute + the influence. So what they gain in one area is potentially offset by what they lose in another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T10:42:39-08:00","id":779938,"title":"","content":"That makes more sense. I didn't notice how Influences only use attribute + influence in Spirit Slayers- guess I kind of glossed over that and my brain went 'Oh, influence rules, I know what these do' and I didn't think about it after that. You know what they say about assumptions. Still, I guess I kind of like the idea of, occasionally, truly god-like spirits.<br /> <br /> In an upcoming Werewolf game I'm planning, I think I'll use this chart for the Spirit Molochinim that the Pure sourcebook says is slumbering in the valley of Hinnom. Pack of PCs show up, thinking it's your average high-Rank Spirit, and then it turns out to be a heck of a lot worse. That'll be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:49:00-08:00","id":779997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777814-spirit-slayers?p=779938#post779938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes more sense. I didn't notice how Influences only use attribute + influence in Spirit Slayers- guess I kind of glossed over that and my brain went 'Oh, influence rules, I know what these do' and I didn't think about it after that. You know what they say about assumptions. Still, I guess I kind of like the idea of, occasionally, truly god-like spirits.<br /> <br /> In an upcoming Werewolf game I'm planning, I think I'll use this chart for the Spirit Molochinim that the Pure sourcebook says is slumbering in the valley of Hinnom. Pack of PCs show up, thinking it's your average high-Rank Spirit, and then it turns out to be a heck of a lot worse. That'll be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, the way Spirit Slayers handles Influences makes them stronger than default Influences - sure, they're rolling less dice, but you can also Strengthen/Control/Create with <i>any</i> number of dots.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:38:54-08:00","id":780055,"title":"","content":"And that is something <i>else </i>I appear to have missed. Being able to Strengthen/Control/Create with even a small Influence seems more in the wheelhouse of Rank 6+ Ephemeral Beings. Might add that as a house rule. High-Rank Ephemeral Beings are utterly terrifying for anything short of a pack of Uratha or a Mage with Mastery in Spirit, aren't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:33:14-08:00","id":780096,"title":"","content":"The closest to rules on how to run rank 6+ entities was in Imperial Mysteries, where it effectively gave rank 6 spirits Mastery in the &quot;their purview&quot; arcarnum (because it was a Mage book) and more powerful ones varying levels or archmastery in same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}